				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/287/949/593/182/322/original/ea34d8a24964f103.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-06-06T18:34:47.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I judge the merit based on problems it solves and “this is fun” reaction. Just as I wouldn’t have bought the first Walkman, first iPhone, first laptop, or first computers - I won’t buy this. But in all cases it’s pretty obvious why those things would become revolutionary and ubiquitous. This is the same. It’s an early clunky expensive version. It’s todays portable Commodore. Give it time.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
