			},
			"date": "2023-06-06T18:38:57.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Importantly; this is *already* viable. It concentrated on 2D workflows and existing compute interfaces. All it does extra is allow infinite screens in any room of any size. Any number of screens in a room the size of your closet. That alone is good. Add to that true 3D stuff; like photos and video; that it’s capable of. Why *wouldn’t* anyone want one, except cost? Virtualise all your *current* screens with one device? Sold. For the right price.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
